(upbeat music)

00:00:52.255 --> 00:00:54.337
- [Interviewer] Did you
ever have, let's call it,

00:00:54.337 --> 00:00:55.894
a normal job, Conor?

00:00:55.894 --> 00:00:56.830
A nine to five?

00:00:56.830 --> 00:00:57.663
- Mm-hm.

00:00:57.663 --> 00:00:59.749
Yeah, 'cause the Irish thing

00:00:59.749 --> 00:01:00.880
is to get into a trade straightaway.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:01.898
I was no different,

00:01:01.898 --> 00:01:04.504
Soon as the day I finished school,

00:01:04.504 --> 00:01:05.533
I was always getting pestered,

00:01:05.533 --> 00:01:06.474
'What're you doing with your life?

00:01:06.474 --> 00:01:08.307
Are you doin' this, doin' that?'

00:01:08.307 --> 00:01:10.319
And they didn't know what it was.

00:01:10.319 --> 00:01:11.914
They didn't know what MMA was,

00:01:11.914 --> 00:01:12.875
they didn't know what none of this,

00:01:12.875 --> 00:01:14.157
they didn't know I could
make a career out of it.

00:01:14.157 --> 00:01:15.058
As far as they were concerned,

00:01:15.058 --> 00:01:16.020
me ma and da I'm talking about,

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:16.853
as far as they were concerned,

00:01:16.853 --> 00:01:17.788
I was just getting into a cage

00:01:17.788 --> 00:01:19.051
and fightin' with some other guy.

00:01:19.051 --> 00:01:20.190
They didn't know nothin' about it.

00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:21.506
No one did really!

00:01:21.506 --> 00:01:22.709
But I knew, you know what I mean?

00:01:22.709 --> 00:01:23.542
I knew!

00:01:24.490 --> 00:01:25.956
And then I ended up getting a trade,

00:01:25.956 --> 00:01:27.391
just to keep them quiet.

00:01:27.391 --> 00:01:29.147
'Cause I used to have a lot
of fights with me da a lot-

00:01:29.147 --> 00:01:30.048
- [Interviewer] What trade did you get?

00:01:30.048 --> 00:01:33.305
- I ended up gettin' a trade as a plumber.

00:01:33.305 --> 00:01:35.531
Literally up in the back guys up an hour

00:01:35.531 --> 00:01:36.713
up in the Wicklow Mountains.

00:01:36.713 --> 00:01:40.428
And that site is one of the
biggest sites in Europe,

00:01:40.428 --> 00:01:43.024
Kilternan was right at that skiin' place.

00:01:43.024 --> 00:01:44.864
Huge, and now it's just abandoned,

00:01:44.864 --> 00:01:46.080
now it's just deserted.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:47.252
So I used to go up there, six o'clock,

00:01:47.252 --> 00:01:49.660
five o'clock in the
morning I was on my M50.

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:51.818
I used to have to walk to the end for,

00:01:51.818 --> 00:01:52.884
about half an hour from me house,

00:01:52.884 --> 00:01:54.827
wait for some limerick guy
that I didn't even know.

00:01:54.827 --> 00:01:57.275
He'd drive on the F4 and
I'd have to flag him down.

00:01:57.275 --> 00:01:58.108
Nightmare, yeah.

00:01:58.108 --> 00:02:00.376
Two hours down on the M50, two hours back.

00:02:00.376 --> 00:02:02.719
Usually 14 hour days and
I was the first year,

00:02:02.719 --> 00:02:04.561
so I had to go and do everything.

00:02:04.561 --> 00:02:07.270
I had to the shop, I had to
go and get this and get that.

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:08.364
So I always had trouble with that

00:02:08.364 --> 00:02:09.681
and I was like this isn't for me.

00:02:09.681 --> 00:02:10.796
This is not for me.

00:02:10.796 --> 00:02:11.959
- [Interviewer] How long did you last?

00:02:11.959 --> 00:02:14.559
- I lasted 18 months doin' it.

00:02:14.559 --> 00:02:16.742
But it was tough, you know?

00:02:16.742 --> 00:02:18.149
Just wasn't the life for me.

00:02:18.149 --> 00:02:20.662
And then John said, 'cause
I was training with John

00:02:20.662 --> 00:02:21.820
as well at the time.

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:23.896
And then John got on twitch and said

00:02:23.896 --> 00:02:26.165
I have a show, I'm running a
show, I'd you to fight in it.

00:02:26.165 --> 00:02:27.084
And then that was it,

00:02:27.084 --> 00:02:28.985
I just packed it in, didn't show up.

00:02:28.985 --> 00:02:30.449
Me da used to come and
punch the head out me,

00:02:30.449 --> 00:02:32.429
like try and drag me out of bed

00:02:32.429 --> 00:02:33.262
and I just wouldn't go.

00:02:33.262 --> 00:02:35.454
You know, I had upper
hour for a good few years

00:02:35.454 --> 00:02:37.121
when I'm miserable.

00:02:38.489 --> 00:02:39.847
And that was it, I just packed it in, quit

00:02:39.847 --> 00:02:41.357
and then focused on trainin'.

00:02:41.357 --> 00:02:43.534
And that's, I knew what
was going to happen.

00:02:43.534 --> 00:02:44.737
I knew I was going to get here.

00:02:44.737 --> 00:02:47.426
They didn't, it was a
lot of stressful years.

00:02:47.426 --> 00:02:48.259
You know what I mean?

00:02:48.259 --> 00:02:50.671
A lot of tough times.

00:02:50.671 --> 00:02:53.745
But I proved them wrong,
I proved myself right.

00:02:53.745 --> 00:02:57.912
- Don't ever let somebody tell
you you can't do something.

00:02:59.477 --> 00:03:00.477
Not even me.

00:03:02.976 --> 00:03:04.447
Alright?

00:03:04.447 --> 00:03:05.280
- Alright.

00:03:06.898 --> 00:03:10.231
- You got a dream, you got to protect it.

00:03:12.637 --> 00:03:14.312
People can't do something themselves,

00:03:14.312 --> 00:03:17.312
they want to tell you you can't do it.

00:03:21.473 --> 00:03:23.799
You want something, go and get it.

00:03:23.799 --> 00:03:24.910
Period.

00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:26.340
- [Interviewer] You're
not against bullying?

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:27.507
- I'm not.

00:03:27.507 --> 00:03:28.340
- [Interviewer] What do you mean?

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:30.205
- I'm not against bullying because

00:03:30.205 --> 00:03:32.133
I feel like the world is bullies.

00:03:32.133 --> 00:03:33.889
Like, there's so many people
who are going to tell you

00:03:33.889 --> 00:03:35.924
that what you're idea is stupid.

00:03:35.924 --> 00:03:37.348
Or you don't belong here

00:03:37.348 --> 00:03:39.659
or you don't deserve certain things.

00:03:39.659 --> 00:03:41.245
- But wouldn't it be a better place-

00:03:41.245 --> 00:03:42.816
- [Donald Glover] If
people didn't do that?

00:03:42.816 --> 00:03:43.914
- But you're saying you're not against it

00:03:43.914 --> 00:03:45.660
'cause it's unrealistic to be against it?

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:48.632
- I'm saying we probably
wouldn't have Kanye West,

00:03:48.632 --> 00:03:51.974
Bill Gates or anyone
without someone being like

00:03:51.974 --> 00:03:53.704
you're not worth it.

00:03:53.704 --> 00:03:55.686
Like we wouldn't have them.

00:03:55.686 --> 00:03:57.972
And like we wouldn't have people

00:03:57.972 --> 00:04:00.041
who were like no, this is worth it.

00:04:00.041 --> 00:04:03.509
Because if everybody's ideas was worth it

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:06.930
and if they felt that way,
everybody felt like that,

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:09.045
we just have, it'd be like nothing.

00:04:09.045 --> 00:04:10.371
Everything would be the same.

00:04:10.371 --> 00:04:12.383
You need somebody to keep being like,

00:04:12.383 --> 00:04:13.352
no, I'm right.

00:04:13.352 --> 00:04:14.453
You need a Joan of Arc, who's like no,

00:04:14.453 --> 00:04:16.283
I'm right, I'm right,
I'm right, I'm right.

00:04:16.283 --> 00:04:18.371
Even if it's crazy, even if it's crazy.

00:04:18.371 --> 00:04:20.820
But then eventually people are
like maybe they're not crazy.

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:22.494
- [Interviewer] Are you that way?

00:04:22.494 --> 00:04:25.587
- I mean, yeah, I like to believe that.

00:04:25.587 --> 00:04:28.649
I mean, people tell me-
- Because you seem like

00:04:28.649 --> 00:04:30.823
such a modest guy when
you're on this show.

00:04:30.823 --> 00:04:32.035
(laughing)

00:04:32.035 --> 00:04:33.511
- [Donald Glover] I'm a salty dude though.

00:04:33.511 --> 00:04:34.344
- Are you?

00:04:34.344 --> 00:04:35.808
- Oh yeah, I remember
everybody who says stuff.

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:38.576
I got beefs with people,
like I remember stuff.

00:04:38.576 --> 00:04:41.437
I remember totally and
most of the things I do,

00:04:41.437 --> 00:04:44.000
it's just like, no I'm right.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:45.386
And I believe in myself more.

00:04:45.386 --> 00:04:46.391
- [Interviewer] You're vengeful?

00:04:46.391 --> 00:04:48.166
- Not vengeful, I'm salty.

00:04:48.166 --> 00:04:48.999
(laughing)
I'm like-

00:04:48.999 --> 00:04:50.054
- What's the difference?

00:04:50.054 --> 00:04:51.512
- The difference would be like.

00:04:51.512 --> 00:04:54.332
Vengeful is like I'm going to
come and destroy you, I think.

00:04:54.332 --> 00:04:55.726
Like, it's like I'm going to wait around-

00:04:55.726 --> 00:04:58.182
- I'm going to, I'm taking
your number down and-

00:04:58.182 --> 00:05:01.208
- And I'm coming for you.
- I'm coming for you.

00:05:01.208 --> 00:05:05.174
- I'm salty, which means I
think salty is a different thing

00:05:05.174 --> 00:05:07.806
because I'm like I'm just
going to prove you wrong.

00:05:07.806 --> 00:05:10.883
I'd much rather you sit there
and be like, huh I was wrong.

00:05:10.883 --> 00:05:13.198
Because then I think that's growing,

00:05:13.198 --> 00:05:14.819
like there's lots of times
where I've done stuff

00:05:14.819 --> 00:05:17.671
and been like I was wrong about
that and I didn't even know.

00:05:17.671 --> 00:05:19.780
And then it makes you
look at things differently

00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:21.822
on experiences in your life.

00:05:21.822 --> 00:05:25.682
Like, I want to make people
think you were wrong.

00:05:25.682 --> 00:05:28.717
- Ignore people telling
you your idea is bad.

00:05:28.717 --> 00:05:30.645
They may be right but the only way to know

00:05:30.645 --> 00:05:32.362
is to actually build it out.

00:05:32.362 --> 00:05:35.975
And I think the thing that
works about Silicon Valley

00:05:35.975 --> 00:05:37.844
that's different than Mexico City

00:05:37.844 --> 00:05:39.829
or almost anywhere else in the world,

00:05:39.829 --> 00:05:42.776
is the default response if someone says

00:05:42.776 --> 00:05:44.984
hey I'm going to start a
start-up, here's my idea.

00:05:44.984 --> 00:05:47.503
The default response is to be excited

00:05:47.503 --> 00:05:50.228
and think like oh why might that work.

00:05:50.228 --> 00:05:52.078
And in most of the rest of the world,

00:05:52.078 --> 00:05:54.236
the default response when
you tell someone your idea

00:05:54.236 --> 00:05:56.616
is to say oh that's not going to work.

00:05:56.616 --> 00:05:59.779
And this is really toxic for start-ups.

00:05:59.779 --> 00:06:01.321
'Cause you have to believe in yourself.

00:06:01.321 --> 00:06:04.344
And the good ideas, because
they sound like bad ideas,

00:06:04.344 --> 00:06:06.844
are so fragile and so killable

00:06:07.772 --> 00:06:09.374
that you have to be really careful

00:06:09.374 --> 00:06:11.413
to insulate yourself against this.

00:06:11.413 --> 00:06:14.663
- When I found some place in my country

00:06:17.190 --> 00:06:20.023
and a lady answered the telephone,

00:06:21.410 --> 00:06:24.410
I then asked, to whom am I speaking?

00:06:26.898 --> 00:06:28.870
She said, you're speaking to me!

00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:31.497
(crowd laughing)

00:06:31.497 --> 00:06:35.286
I said, well lady, I
know I'm speaking to you.

00:06:35.286 --> 00:06:37.384
But what's your name?

00:06:37.384 --> 00:06:39.325
She said, who are you to ask for my name?

00:06:39.325 --> 00:06:40.359
What's your name?

00:06:40.359 --> 00:06:43.165
(crowd laughing)

00:06:43.165 --> 00:06:46.884
I say, well lady, as soon
as you tell me your name

00:06:46.884 --> 00:06:48.467
I'll tell you mine.

00:06:49.337 --> 00:06:52.131
But as we argued as to who should tell

00:06:52.131 --> 00:06:54.569
(crowd laughing)
his or her name,

00:06:54.569 --> 00:06:57.993
she became very cross and she said,

00:06:57.993 --> 00:07:00.070
you seem to be a backward person

00:07:00.070 --> 00:07:01.581
(crowd laughing)

00:07:01.581 --> 00:07:02.414
have you passed your matric?

00:07:02.414 --> 00:07:04.564
(crowd laughing)

00:07:04.564 --> 00:07:08.731
Now matric in our country is a
university entry examination.

00:07:10.587 --> 00:07:14.357
And I said, well lady,
you must be very careful.

00:07:14.357 --> 00:07:17.157
Because if the qualification
to speak to you

00:07:17.157 --> 00:07:20.555
is the possession of a matric certificate,

00:07:20.555 --> 00:07:24.374
I might work hard and pass my matric

00:07:24.374 --> 00:07:27.374
and be in the same class as you are.

00:07:28.719 --> 00:07:30.136
That was treason.

00:07:31.431 --> 00:07:34.681
She said, you will never be in my class

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:37.819
and banged the telephone.

00:07:37.819 --> 00:07:40.687
(crowd laughing)

00:07:40.687 --> 00:07:43.531
How I wish she were here today.

00:07:43.531 --> 00:07:47.364
(crowd laughing and cheering)

00:08:00.261 --> 00:08:04.261
She would now discover
that I have achieved more

00:08:05.199 --> 00:08:07.034
than passed my matric.

00:08:07.034 --> 00:08:09.024
- And you know when they say

00:08:09.024 --> 00:08:13.067
oh I would like you to do this for me or,

00:08:13.067 --> 00:08:16.355
and I produce a lot of
first time filmmakers

00:08:16.355 --> 00:08:18.553
but I don't produce all
first time filmmakers

00:08:18.553 --> 00:08:19.386
that approach me.

00:08:19.386 --> 00:08:23.683
And I say look if I say no and you give up

00:08:23.683 --> 00:08:26.921
I'm sorry to tell you but
it's the wrong job for you

00:08:26.921 --> 00:08:30.524
'cause you live with rejection for decades

00:08:30.524 --> 00:08:32.556
sometimes as a director.

00:08:32.556 --> 00:08:34.925
And you end up making the
movie you want to make

00:08:34.925 --> 00:08:38.664
so if I say no that doesn't mean I'm right

00:08:38.664 --> 00:08:41.920
or I'm wrong, you just say f him,

00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:43.533
I'll show him later, you know.

00:08:43.533 --> 00:08:46.464
I'm going to make it and
that fat bastard is going to

00:08:46.464 --> 00:08:51.235
have to say I was so wrong
and hit himself in the head

00:08:51.235 --> 00:08:52.768
because he didn't do it.

00:08:52.768 --> 00:08:54.691
And I think that's the thing to do,

00:08:54.691 --> 00:08:57.523
is show us, don't tell us you know.

00:08:57.523 --> 00:08:59.205
Do the things.

00:08:59.205 --> 00:09:02.939
And if you do them wrong but
you do I mean your own terms,

00:09:02.939 --> 00:09:04.603
that's how I define success.

00:09:04.603 --> 00:09:06.491
Failing in your own terms.

00:09:06.491 --> 00:09:10.281
- Do you think that
people underestimate you?

00:09:10.281 --> 00:09:12.652
Underestimate your how much
you work on this stuff,

00:09:12.652 --> 00:09:14.261
underestimate your intelligence?

00:09:14.261 --> 00:09:17.249
And my question is is that
something you push back on

00:09:17.249 --> 00:09:20.223
or something you leverage?

00:09:20.223 --> 00:09:22.613
- Definitely something
that doesn't bother me.

00:09:22.613 --> 00:09:24.452
- [Interviewer] Okay.

00:09:24.452 --> 00:09:27.434
- When someone underestimates me,

00:09:27.434 --> 00:09:30.701
I love to get to know them and have them

00:09:30.701 --> 00:09:33.431
have one conversation with me

00:09:33.431 --> 00:09:36.601
to just understand that it's,

00:09:36.601 --> 00:09:38.568
I mean I think the
easiest question to ask is

00:09:38.568 --> 00:09:39.795
what does she do?

00:09:39.795 --> 00:09:41.745
What is your talent, you know?

00:09:41.745 --> 00:09:46.184
And I jokingly said, actually
to my husband the other day,

00:09:46.184 --> 00:09:47.305
I said, you know what?

00:09:47.305 --> 00:09:50.274
My next answer should be, sarcastically,

00:09:50.274 --> 00:09:52.885
how lucky am I if I don't
sing and I don't dance

00:09:52.885 --> 00:09:55.685
but I'm still doing what I'm doing,

00:09:55.685 --> 00:09:56.815
how easy is my job?

00:09:56.815 --> 00:09:57.795
I don't have to do any of that.

00:09:57.795 --> 00:10:00.683
I don't have to be on stage
like you working so hard

00:10:00.683 --> 00:10:03.243
but we're still driving the same car,

00:10:03.243 --> 00:10:04.399
we're still living the same life.

00:10:04.399 --> 00:10:05.539
(crowd laughing)

00:10:05.539 --> 00:10:08.289
So lucky me, if it was that easy.

00:10:09.798 --> 00:10:12.257
But you know, I think it's
just the easiest thing to ask.

00:10:12.257 --> 00:10:15.977
For anyone to really assume
that it's not a full-time job

00:10:15.977 --> 00:10:18.644
to have to sit and create things

00:10:20.031 --> 00:10:23.180
and come up with every single blog post

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:24.777
and I do, you know, three a day

00:10:24.777 --> 00:10:28.677
and having to you know, working on apps.

00:10:28.677 --> 00:10:31.117
To me, it would be the
same thing as people saying

00:10:31.117 --> 00:10:32.390
like anything blogging.

00:10:32.390 --> 00:10:33.339
Like, what do you do?

00:10:33.339 --> 00:10:34.472
You're sitting at home in your apartment

00:10:34.472 --> 00:10:36.313
and you're just on the computer.

00:10:36.313 --> 00:10:37.414
Like that is such-
- I think people do

00:10:37.414 --> 00:10:39.752
say things that about us.
- hard work, you know?

00:10:39.752 --> 00:10:42.032
And I respect it so much, you know?

00:10:42.032 --> 00:10:44.157
And they say that about
the modeling world.

00:10:44.157 --> 00:10:45.660
Well, they just sit there looking pretty.

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:48.809
It is a full-time job for models

00:10:48.809 --> 00:10:51.226
like my sister even, Kendall.

00:10:53.415 --> 00:10:56.832
It's, I don't mind getting underestimated

00:10:58.047 --> 00:11:01.630
but I feel for people
that I understand how

00:11:02.637 --> 00:11:06.853
it could bother them if they
were put in the same situation.

00:11:06.853 --> 00:11:09.951
Even filming a reality
show, it's a full-time job.

00:11:09.951 --> 00:11:13.338
I think that, I know reality shows

00:11:13.338 --> 00:11:16.498
don't get the respect that
I believe they deserve

00:11:16.498 --> 00:11:18.949
and that's why I love
being on one for so long

00:11:18.949 --> 00:11:23.710
and I will always fight to
be on as long as possible

00:11:23.710 --> 00:11:25.898
because I love to show and prove

00:11:25.898 --> 00:11:30.318
but my personality is just
if you underestimate me

00:11:30.318 --> 00:11:32.606
I would love to have a
conversation with you.

00:11:32.606 --> 00:11:37.048
I would love to, I just
like to prove people wrong.

00:11:37.048 --> 00:11:40.845
- But I was dumping the
pasta one night into the sink

00:11:40.845 --> 00:11:44.516
and all of a sudden Ramon Simone walks in

00:11:44.516 --> 00:11:45.573
and he says you know Barbara

00:11:45.573 --> 00:11:47.655
we have something serious to discuss.

00:11:47.655 --> 00:11:49.939
I'm going to marry your secretary.

00:11:49.939 --> 00:11:50.772
My Tina?

00:11:52.616 --> 00:11:54.620
She went from Tina the
wonderful secretary,

00:11:54.620 --> 00:11:57.261
I won't even put a label on her.

00:11:57.261 --> 00:12:00.796
I just couldn't believe
my ears or my eyes.

00:12:00.796 --> 00:12:03.618
I'm like what, how's that possible?

00:12:03.618 --> 00:12:04.614
He said take your time moving out.

00:12:04.614 --> 00:12:07.965
I took about a minute,
grabbed a toothbrush,

00:12:07.965 --> 00:12:09.330
and walked out the door

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:10.926
and moved in with my girlfriend Kathy

00:12:10.926 --> 00:12:12.946
who was living on East
79th Street in a studio

00:12:12.946 --> 00:12:16.909
and she let me stay there 'til
I got my feet back under me.

00:12:16.909 --> 00:12:19.248
I should say that for the
first time in my life,

00:12:19.248 --> 00:12:20.413
I don't know what hit me.

00:12:20.413 --> 00:12:21.387
I guess that hit me.

00:12:21.387 --> 00:12:23.510
But I can't believe I managed it so badly.

00:12:23.510 --> 00:12:24.926
I felt like I was a nobody.

00:12:24.926 --> 00:12:27.260
I went from a somebody
with a successful business

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:31.041
to a nobody because I was
turned down for a younger woman.

00:12:31.041 --> 00:12:33.409
Tina was five years younger than me.

00:12:33.409 --> 00:12:35.529
I had to admit, she was prettier.

00:12:35.529 --> 00:12:37.171
She had real blonde hair.

00:12:37.171 --> 00:12:38.285
I was already highlighting.

00:12:38.285 --> 00:12:39.848
(crowd laughing)

00:12:39.848 --> 00:12:41.715
I hated her for that.

00:12:41.715 --> 00:12:43.715
She was calm and pretty.

00:12:45.467 --> 00:12:46.665
I hated her.

00:12:46.665 --> 00:12:48.298
(crowd laughing)

00:12:48.298 --> 00:12:50.158
But I went to work every day.

00:12:50.158 --> 00:12:52.025
I wanted to fire Tina but Ray reminded me

00:12:52.025 --> 00:12:53.339
he was the controlling partner.

00:12:53.339 --> 00:12:54.226
I couldn't do that.

00:12:54.226 --> 00:12:56.490
Tina moved into my desk in Ray's office

00:12:56.490 --> 00:12:58.893
where I used to sit and I sat
out with the sales people.

00:12:58.893 --> 00:13:01.115
And every day I went in
smiling like a puppet

00:13:01.115 --> 00:13:02.909
but in my heart I was runnin' around

00:13:02.909 --> 00:13:05.232
a broken heart and loss of confidence.

00:13:05.232 --> 00:13:07.830
I just thought to myself my god,

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:09.872
I was nothing before Ray found me.

00:13:09.872 --> 00:13:11.502
He picked me up, found me.

00:13:11.502 --> 00:13:13.569
He was my mentor, he gave me confidence,

00:13:13.569 --> 00:13:14.922
he gave me the money
to start the business.

00:13:14.922 --> 00:13:17.228
Everything good that had changed my life,

00:13:17.228 --> 00:13:20.161
all led to one place
which was Ramon Simone.

00:13:20.161 --> 00:13:24.081
And I thought he's right, I'll
never succeed without him.

00:13:24.081 --> 00:13:26.548
But I can't even remember
what clicked in my head,

00:13:26.548 --> 00:13:29.397
maybe desperation, but
one day I just decided

00:13:29.397 --> 00:13:30.530
I'm not going to do this anymore.

00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:32.943
And I walked in and I
said to Ramone Simone,

00:13:32.943 --> 00:13:34.169
you know what, I'm ending this business

00:13:34.169 --> 00:13:35.353
and here's how we're going to do it.

00:13:35.353 --> 00:13:37.921
We're going to chop up the 14
salespeople like a football draw.

00:13:37.921 --> 00:13:39.670
You can pick the first
person, I'll pick the second.

00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:40.919
We'll do it fair.

00:13:40.919 --> 00:13:42.024
If you want to move out, you can move out.

00:13:42.024 --> 00:13:43.557
If you want me to move out, no problem.

00:13:43.557 --> 00:13:45.050
You want to keep the
phone number, no problem.

00:13:45.050 --> 00:13:46.687
Or I'll get a new phone number.

00:13:46.687 --> 00:13:47.520
Whatever.

00:13:47.520 --> 00:13:48.852
You go first.

00:13:48.852 --> 00:13:51.560
He picked Norma Hirsch,
our star salesperson.

00:13:51.560 --> 00:13:54.208
I picked Ester Kaplan, our
not-so-star salesperson

00:13:54.208 --> 00:13:55.408
but I had a plan for her.

00:13:55.408 --> 00:13:57.157
And we went right down the line

00:13:57.157 --> 00:13:59.552
and I would say within maybe six minutes,

00:13:59.552 --> 00:14:00.542
we ended a partnership.

00:14:00.542 --> 00:14:01.375
Boom!

00:14:01.375 --> 00:14:02.208
Like that.

00:14:02.208 --> 00:14:04.189
We had $37,000 in cash.

00:14:04.189 --> 00:14:07.102
He wrote me a check for half of $37,000

00:14:07.102 --> 00:14:08.398
and as luck would have it,

00:14:08.398 --> 00:14:12.040
it was a real estate recession
we're just about to dive into

00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:13.158
and why was it great?

00:14:13.158 --> 00:14:15.415
Because commercial space
wasn't leasing well.

00:14:15.415 --> 00:14:18.933
He was on the eighth floor,
where my old office was.

00:14:18.933 --> 00:14:21.558
I rented the identical
space on the eleventh floor

00:14:21.558 --> 00:14:23.653
above him, there was a little ego in that

00:14:23.653 --> 00:14:24.615
I'm sorry to say.

00:14:24.615 --> 00:14:27.793
How needy was I?
(crowd laughing)

00:14:27.793 --> 00:14:30.396
And by Monday, this was on a Thursday,

00:14:30.396 --> 00:14:32.321
by Monday, I moved my salespeople in

00:14:32.321 --> 00:14:33.154
'cause in those times,

00:14:33.154 --> 00:14:35.344
you could rent black
desks, rent phones, bang!

00:14:35.344 --> 00:14:37.817
We were in operation and my
seven salespeople moved in

00:14:37.817 --> 00:14:40.311
and that was the birth
of the Corcoran Group.

00:14:40.311 --> 00:14:43.618
Right before I left Ramon
Simone's office that day,

00:14:43.618 --> 00:14:46.142
or should I say Ray and
Tina's office that day.

00:14:46.142 --> 00:14:47.643
And by the way, you know
what his real name was?

00:14:47.643 --> 00:14:48.775
It wasn't even Ramon Simone.

00:14:48.775 --> 00:14:49.924
I found out from his mother Vicky

00:14:49.924 --> 00:14:52.082
his real name was Ray Simon.

00:14:52.082 --> 00:14:54.452
And he wasn't from the Basque
country like he always told me

00:14:54.452 --> 00:14:57.043
he was from 145th Street
in Harlem, go figure.

00:14:57.043 --> 00:14:59.793
(crowd laughing)

00:15:00.868 --> 00:15:01.784
Alrighty.

00:15:01.784 --> 00:15:04.379
Well anyway, so right
before I left the office,

00:15:04.379 --> 00:15:06.604
that's when Ray gave me
the gift of a lifetime

00:15:06.604 --> 00:15:08.384
when he said to me those words

00:15:08.384 --> 00:15:10.438
that reflected in my head
for the rest of my life.

00:15:10.438 --> 00:15:11.650
It still gets me goin'.

00:15:11.650 --> 00:15:14.317
You'll never succeed without me.

00:15:15.245 --> 00:15:17.578
I'm telling you, I don't
believe in negative motivation.

00:15:17.578 --> 00:15:19.827
I'm a positive person like my mother.

00:15:19.827 --> 00:15:22.650
But he really knew my number.

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:24.455
If he had said I know
you're going to be amazing,

00:15:24.455 --> 00:15:25.910
I'm sure I wouldn't
have stayed in business

00:15:25.910 --> 00:15:27.308
in the tough times.

00:15:27.308 --> 00:15:30.926
But it was that scolding
tattoo in my heart:

00:15:30.926 --> 00:15:33.104
you'll never succeed without me.

00:15:33.104 --> 00:15:35.363
That every time I was near-death,

00:15:35.363 --> 00:15:37.098
growing my business
through the ups and downs

00:15:37.098 --> 00:15:38.386
of the real estate recession.

00:15:38.386 --> 00:15:41.633
Being overextended, being
over leverage, owing money.

00:15:41.633 --> 00:15:42.704
Blah blah blah.

00:15:42.704 --> 00:15:46.054
That same phrase got me goin' again.

00:15:46.054 --> 00:15:50.716
He gave me an insurance policy
for success by insulting me.

00:15:50.716 --> 00:15:52.611
Thank god he did.

00:15:52.611 --> 00:15:54.165
I have thanked him a million times.

00:15:54.165 --> 00:15:55.577
What happened to Ramon Simone?

00:15:55.577 --> 00:15:57.641
He married Tina, they
have three kids together.

00:15:57.641 --> 00:15:59.494
They are so much more happily married

00:15:59.494 --> 00:16:01.082
than myself and my husband, Bill.

00:16:01.082 --> 00:16:02.120
They were meant to be together.

00:16:02.120 --> 00:16:03.422
(crowd laughing)

00:16:03.422 --> 00:16:06.264
They were destined, okay?

00:16:06.264 --> 00:16:09.023
But still, thank god
he gave me that insult

00:16:09.023 --> 00:16:12.289
to insure my success
for the rest of my life.

00:16:12.289 --> 00:16:15.543
- Do not listen to the naysayers.

00:16:15.543 --> 00:16:19.075
If you are going to have a breakthrough,

00:16:19.075 --> 00:16:23.693
you've got to be able to
silence the negative voices.

00:16:23.693 --> 00:16:26.499
That's the next step and
that's the next secret.

00:16:26.499 --> 00:16:31.486
Many of us have too many
people speaking into our ears.

00:16:31.486 --> 00:16:34.484
I just called these people abortionists.

00:16:34.484 --> 00:16:36.328
So you've got to be careful.

00:16:36.328 --> 00:16:39.485
Your dreams, your visions, your desires.

00:16:39.485 --> 00:16:41.934
Especially those that have been god-given.

00:16:41.934 --> 00:16:43.574
I want you to pursue them.

00:16:43.574 --> 00:16:48.227
I want you to believe that
all things are possible.

00:16:48.227 --> 00:16:50.610
It is possible for you
to go back to school.

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:54.090
It is possible for you to
heal your relationship.

00:16:54.090 --> 00:16:57.757
It is possible for you
to go at life alone.

00:16:57.757 --> 00:16:59.644
It is possible.

00:16:59.644 --> 00:17:02.082
- Seems to be that managers
from other countries come

00:17:02.082 --> 00:17:04.646
and they are quickly
addicted to the place.

00:17:04.646 --> 00:17:05.479
- [Pep Guardiola] Yeah.

00:17:05.479 --> 00:17:06.745
- Have you spoke to
anybody on that behalf.

00:17:06.745 --> 00:17:08.862
- Yeah, they told me
it's so hard, so tough.

00:17:08.862 --> 00:17:13.683
And all the people say
Pep is not going to adapt

00:17:13.683 --> 00:17:16.464
and coach in that way,
so that is why I'm here.

00:17:16.464 --> 00:17:19.613
To try to do it so the people have

00:17:19.613 --> 00:17:22.476
some of them confident it's going well,

00:17:22.476 --> 00:17:25.393
but some of them in Germany as well

00:17:26.391 --> 00:17:30.234
the people say the way you
play is not possible here

00:17:30.234 --> 00:17:31.739
in the Premier League so.

00:17:31.739 --> 00:17:34.017
And I said myself why not?

00:17:34.017 --> 00:17:38.183
Why we don't travel there
to try it and that's why.

00:17:38.183 --> 00:17:40.594
So it's a big challenge, not just for me

00:17:40.594 --> 00:17:45.477
but I am always in my teams I
was able to emboss the players

00:17:45.477 --> 00:17:47.595
and it went to help us here as well.

00:17:47.595 --> 00:17:50.082
When that's happened,
everything will be easy.

00:17:50.082 --> 00:17:51.607
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:17:51.607 --> 00:17:52.868
I hope you enjoyed the video.

00:17:52.868 --> 00:17:54.568
I'd love to know what did you think?

00:17:54.568 --> 00:17:56.581
What was the single biggest
takeaway that you took

00:17:56.581 --> 00:17:58.496
from this video that you're going to apply

00:17:58.496 --> 00:18:00.543
to your life or to your business somehow?

00:18:00.543 --> 00:18:02.175
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:18:02.175 --> 00:18:03.526
If you're within the first couple hours

00:18:03.526 --> 00:18:04.535
of this video going live,

00:18:04.535 --> 00:18:07.043
you have a chance to win one
of two daily prizes as well.

00:18:07.043 --> 00:18:09.390
I also want to give a
quick shout out to Eduardo.

00:18:09.390 --> 00:18:11.689
Eduardo, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:18:11.689 --> 00:18:13.414
Your One Word, and taking that picture

00:18:13.414 --> 00:18:14.830
and posting it to Facebook.

00:18:14.830 --> 00:18:17.036
I really appreciate the support, man.

00:18:17.036 --> 00:18:18.004
And I hope you enjoyed the read.

00:18:18.004 --> 00:18:19.324
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:18:19.324 --> 00:18:20.499
I believe in you.

00:18:20.499 --> 00:18:22.584
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:18:22.584 --> 00:18:24.583
and whatever your one word is.

00:18:24.583 --> 00:18:26.638
Much love, I'll see you soon.

00:18:26.638 --> 00:18:28.971
(swooshing)

